  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YALI Kiprotich Slopes Of Mount Elgon Honey</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agribusiness .Beneficiaries: YALI Youth 277 of which 136 are women..Trainees/Interns = 3.Suppliers = 150.Distrbutiors = 3.Customers = 106.Jobs Created = 10.Community members trained = 5 ...Slopes of Mount Elgon Honey will increase monthly production and will expand their workforce by training and hiring 10 disabled persons to own 6 beehives improving their livelihoods and increasing honey production. The purpose of the Project is to increase job creation for marginalized individuals and the utilization of land that is otherwise deemed as unfit for agriculture into an environmentally sustainable and economically viable product in the apiculture of Uganda. ..USADF grant funds will be used to: (a) expand production with 60 additional hives; (b) establish a processing plant; (c) purchase of a moto to increase distribution; and (d) staff training and capacity building. .</narrative>
  </description>
